{"segs": ["PA_ja_46:0.2", "PA_ja_46:0.3"], "en": "Ekakanipāta, Atthakāmavagga (The Section on Those Desiring Welfare)", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_46:0.4", "PA_ja_46:1.1"], "en": "6. The Ārāmadūsakajātaka “Indeed, for one who is unskilled in what is beneficial,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_46:1.2"], "en": "conduct aimed at the welfare of others does not bring happiness.”", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_46:1.3"], "en": "“The fool ruins his own welfare,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_46:1.4"], "en": "just like the monkey who was a park-keeper.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_46:2.1"], "en": "Thus ends the sixth Jātaka, the Ārāmadūsaka-jātaka.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"}
